snowplow-identities 0.2.0 (2026-YY-ZZ)
---------------------------------------
See MIGRATION.md for upgrade steps and rebuild recipes for the removed tables.

Breaking changes
- `snowplow_identities_id_changes` removed. Rebuild recipe in MIGRATION.md.
- `snowplow_identities_id_mapping_scd` removed. Rebuild recipe in MIGRATION.md.
- `snowplow_identities_new_identities` renamed to `snowplow_identities_identities`,
  and its per-identifier columns (domain_userid, user_id, ...) removed. Those values
  live in `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping` at the identifier grain, which keeps
  every value an identity has carried instead of collapsing to one per type.

Changed
- `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping` is now a view over the new
  `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping_base` table, resolving each row to its current
  `active_snowplow_id` at read time. Columns, grain and values are unchanged, so
  consumers need no changes.
- Each model now tracks its own progress off its own `max(load_tstamp)` instead of a
  shared manifest. This retires the manifest table, the base layer, the whole `_this_run`
  scratch layer and every run hook: 15 models become 5 plus a view, and every dependency
  is a real `ref()` visible in the dbt lineage graph. All derived tables gain a
  `load_tstamp` column, so upgrading replays history once from `snowplow__start_date`.
- `snowplow__allow_refresh`, `snowplow__dev_target_name` and the `models_to_remove` var
  are removed with the manifest. `--full-refresh` now just rebuilds from
  `snowplow__start_date`.

Added
- Run-window logging. Every model logs its watermark and the window it is processing,
  replacing the manifest framework's `print_run_limits` output.
- `snowplow_id_models_in_sync` test, failing when any model's watermark trails the
  furthest-ahead model by more than `snowplow__max_watermark_drift_days` (default 7).
  Without a shared manifest nothing else surfaces a model that has quietly fallen behind.
- `snowplow__lookback_days` (default 1), the overlap re-scanned each run for late-arriving
  data and the window over which re-running a batch is a no-op.
- `snowplow__partition_tstamp`, `snowplow__partition_tstamp_type` and
  `snowplow__partition_buffer_days`, so staging scans prune correctly when
  `atomic.events` is partitioned on something other than `load_tstamp`.

Fixed
- Merges no longer rewrite, re-point or delete identifier rows. `identifier_mapping_base`
  is keyed on an immutable surrogate of (snowplow_id, id_type, id_value), which makes the
  recurring re-pointing failures unrepresentable: stale rows after cascading merges,
  duplicate keys for shared identifiers, and the duplicate-uuid MERGE error.
- An identifier that expires from the identity engine and later reappears under a new
  identity now keeps both rows rather than overwriting the first.
- `merge_events` no longer applies `snowplow__app_id` to `identity_merge` events. Those are
  emitted by the identity service under the `snowplow-identities` app_id, so filtering them
  by a customer's own app ids dropped every merge event and silently stopped identity
  resolution. They are now always filtered to `snowplow-identities`.

Removed
- The `snowplow_identities_snowplow_id_mapping_affected` pre-hook snapshot table and the
  `snowplow_identities_internal` source that read it without a DAG edge.
- The `delete_stale_identifier_mapping_rows` macro and its post-hook.

